  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 clearly outperforms pca_n2000 in the RNA-only setting (0.520 vs 0.485, ~3.5% gap), and the current best result is multimodal with pca_n2000+resnet50+concat (0.527), which barely exceeds scvi RNA-only. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether the RNA encoder advantage carries into the multimodal setting, and whether the modest image contribution from resnet50 is sufficient to justify the added complexity. This experiment (config_028: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_016, isolating the RNA encoder effect in the multimodal context. If it substantially beats 0.527, it confirms scvi_n200 is the right backbone for further multimodal exploration; if it plateaus near 0.520, it signals that resnet50 adds little and we should pivot to a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or multiprofile strategies. Under a tight budget, this is the highest-information next step because it directly extends the strongest observed signal (better RNA encoder) into the most promising model family (multimodal) while keeping all other variables fixed for a clean attribution."
}

